<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29809" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δωρ-ιστί</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in Dorian fashion</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δ. ζῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					336c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>in the Dorian dialect</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαλοῦσι Δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Iamb.</u>
					1.354
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Δ. ἁρμονία</span> the
			<u>Dorian</u> mode or measure in music, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1340b4
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δ.</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				399a
			</span></i>; in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				989
			</span></i> (lyr.) with a play on <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρον</span>.</div>
